    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $q$ denote the projection from $\calD $ to a point. We note that both $(1)$ and $(2)$ imply that $p(f)$ is an equivalence in $\calD $, and therefore $q$-Cartesian by $(\ast )$. The equivalence of $(1)$ and $(2)$ now follows from $(\ast )$ and the third part of Proposition <a href="/tag/D69CB9" data-tag="D69CB9">2.4.1.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
